;; ============================================================================
;; VERIFICATION DOCUMENT — useq-perform
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; This buffer is the single verification surface for the app. Load it in the
;; main editor and step through each row using the verification harness toolbar
;; (top-bar "Verify" button). Each row defines:
;;
;;   - A starting state (code + cursor position marked with |)
;;   - An action to fire (by ActionId)
;;   - An expected post-state (code + cursor position marked with |)
;;   - Pass/fail status (persisted to localStorage via the persistence service)
;;
;; Cursor marker convention:
;;   | = cursor position (zero-width)
;;   |[...]| = selection (from left | to right |)
;;
;; How to run verification:
;;   1. Open this file in the main editor (File > Open or drag-drop)
;;   2. Click the "Verify" toolbar button (or gamepad: LB+Back)
;;   3. The harness walks each row: it sets up the starting state,
;;      waits for you to fire the action (keyboard/gamepad/Go button),
;;      then compares the result against the expected post-state.
;;   4. Mark pass/fail. Results persist across sessions.
;;
;; Row format:
;;   ;; @verify <category> <action-id>
;;   ;; @before <code-with-cursor>
;;   ;; @after  <code-with-cursor>
;;   ;; @status <pass|fail|skip|pending>
;;   ;; @notes  <optional notes>
;;
;; ============================================================================

;; ============================================================================
;; CATEGORY: Navigation
;; ============================================================================
;; These checks verify cursor movement in structural and character modes.
;; The Navigation group is the foundation — all other groups depend on the
;; cursor being in the right place.

